- op: discuss  # 0e5b
  at: '2026-09-21T00:16:17Z'  # 0e5b
  by: agent  # 0e5b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 0e5b
  clock: 5  # 0e5b
  nonce: 0e5b  # 0e5b
  message: "DEFECT 2 EXPLAINED AND FIXED. It was not a parsing bug in the step and not manifest growth: the step read a file that a SIBLING STEP had overwritten.\n\nTHE ARITHMETIC THAT CRACKED IT. 964 is exactly\n\n    find packages/*/tests tests \\( -name 'test_*.py' -o -name 'BRANCHES_test_*.py' \\) -type f | wc -l\n\n= 848 + 116 at 0cb9039d39 -- smart-test's FULL-SUITE manifest writer, verbatim. The original filing ruled the full-suite fallback out by counting 850 test files and observing 964 > 850. That count was test_*.py only; the writer's find also takes the 116 BRANCHES_test_*.py. A wrong instrument returns a plausible number, not an error (L44).\n\nGROUND TRUTH, from the CI logs rather than reasoning:\n    0cb9039d39  (PR #1107 round 1)  === pytest (964 selected files, -n 8) ===   29677 tests\n    e9acc336bb  (PR #1106)          === pytest (71 selected files, -n 8) ===     2322 tests\n    97a128fcb4  (PR #1107 final)    === pytest (282 selected files, -n 8) ===    9663 tests\n71 and 282 match their committed manifests exactly. Only round 1 diverged, and 0cb9039d39's parent IS dev's head 9565972d49, so the checked-out tree carried the 75-path manifest. The workspace file was not the committed file.\n\nROOT CAUSE. scripts/smart-test decides which repo it is talking about from its OWN location -- REPO_ROOT=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")/..\" && pwd)\", then cd \"$REPO_ROOT\" at line 35 -- and writes the literal relative path .ci/affected-tests.txt. The caller's cwd never enters the decision. So /A/scripts/smart-test run from inside repo /B does not produce /B's manifest and does not fail: it rewrites /A's COMMITTED artifact, silently.\n\nREPRODUCED, before the fix (cwd = a throwaway git repo):\n    $ md5sum .ci/affected-tests.txt          -> 6fa7576977b0ca4083d99ec1576ff283\n    $ cd /tmp/foreign && bash ~/hypergumbo/scripts/smart-test --manifest\n    $ ls /tmp/foreign/.ci                    -> No such file or directory\n    $ md5sum ~/hypergumbo/.ci/affected-tests.txt -> ebc945166b241f9eb09bfabe4b582260\nThe foreign repo got nothing; the real repo's committed manifest was rewritten.\n\nTHE PATH INTO CI. Ten tests/test_autopr_*.py modules drive the real scripts/auto-pr with cwd set to a fixture repo and WITHOUT AUTO_PR_SKIP_MANIFEST=1; auto-pr regenerates the manifest before pushing. The Woodpecker steps share ONE workspace. forge-arms (depends_on: []) installs pytest and nothing else and runs tests/test_autopr_*.py -- verified in its log at 0cb9039d39: \"pip install pytest\", then 339 passed in 82s. With no hypergumbo on PATH the regen took smart-test's \"no stable hypergumbo found\" branch -> run_full_suite -> a 964-entry manifest written over the checked-out one. The pytest step waits on build-grammars and ran much later, so it read the clobbered file.\n\nWHY IT LOOKED INEXPLICABLE. tests/test_autopr_mode_declaration.py was made hermetic in 0f0f345415 (the mode-gate tests now run from branch=\"dev\", which exits at auto-pr's protected-branch check BEFORE the manifest regen). The symptom vanished on its own between rounds 1 and 5, so nothing reproduced it afterwards.\n\nFIXED AT THE WRITER (scripts/smart-test, not a governance file). A cwd inside a DIFFERENT git repo is refused with exit 3, naming both roots and both ways out. Scoped to the case shown to bite: a cwd in no git repo names no competing manifest and keeps today's behaviour. Verified against the original repro -- refusal printed, exit 3, real manifest byte-identical (md5 6fa757... unchanged).\n\nFIXED AT THE READER TOO (.woodpecker/woodpecker.yml, not governance). The pytest step now reads the blob committed at HEAD, prints the HEADER of the manifest it actually read (the filed next step -- the old output was a count, which is untraceable to a file), and discloses any disagreement between disk and HEAD. It DISCLOSES rather than fails: measuring the committed artifact is the safety property, and turning an unexplained rewrite into a red PR is the recall-loss direction.\n\nTESTS. tests/test_smart_test_foreign_repo.py (4, new): the regression, the refusal's content, plus two difference arms -- an in-repo cwd still writes, and a non-repo cwd is not treated as foreign. They build a disposable repo owning a COPY of smart-test, so the red state cannot damage the real manifest. tests/test_ci_pytest_selection_gate.py (+5): the gate reads the committed blob, the divergence is disclosed, an undisturbed manifest is NOT flagged (mutation-tested -- making the warning unconditional turns it red), the header is printed, and an unreadable HEAD blob falls back while saying so.\n\nLocal: 410 passed across the auto-pr/smart-test/CI slice, 1996 passed across the full affected slice.\n\nNOT ASSERTED. The general claim \"no other step rewrites the workspace\" is not made; the reader-side disclosure is there precisely because a second writer would otherwise be invisible again. RESIDUAL FILED as WI-furum: auto-pr discards smart-test's stderr, so the refusal is invisible to an auto-pr caller, who sees \"no stable hypergumbo?\" instead -- one message carrying three causes. That fix touches scripts/auto-pr (governance) and is filed needs_human_review."  # 0e5b
- op: discuss  # ae09
  at: '2026-09-21T00:22:00Z'  # ae09
  by: agent  # ae09
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ae09
  clock: 6  # ae09
  nonce: ae09  # ae09
  message: "MERGED as PR #1110, dev 8b68270428.\n\nLIVE EVIDENCE for the READER half, from this PR's own pytest step (4446fe3af5):\n\n    === manifest read by this step ===\n      # Mode: targeted\n      # Selected tests: 119\n    === pytest (119 selected files, -n 8) ===\n\nThe header is printed, and 119 matches the blob committed at that SHA exactly. No divergence warning fired, so the workspace manifest agreed with HEAD.\n\nWHAT THAT LAST LINE DOES NOT PROVE, stated so nobody reads it as more than it is. A clean read is NOT by itself evidence that the writer guard fired inside that pipeline: #1107's FINAL round (97a128fc) also ran tests/test_autopr_*.py in forge-arms and read 282 == committed, with no guard present, because the one test that reached auto-pr's manifest regen had already been made hermetic. And auto-pr discards smart-test's stderr (WI-furum), so a refusal in CI leaves no trace to grep for. The writer guard is established by the local repro (real manifest byte-identical after a foreign-cwd call that previously rewrote it, exit 3) and by the four tests in tests/test_smart_test_foreign_repo.py -- not by this pipeline."  # ae09
